From 315af345ed087991a8a851ceda2d697f7fc2a14a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:06:17 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 33/34] fix(desktop): second review of the 1.7.0 fixes

Backend
- Never delete stored captures on a partial view: startup and discard
  cleanup run only when every batch manifest was read, so a manifest held
  by a scanner or damaged no longer costs its batch's reviewed captures.
- ZIP pre-check uses zipfile's own end-record reader (ZIP64 applied as the
  parser applies it) and caps the central directory at 6 MiB; a lying plain
  end record can no longer hide a million-entry directory.
- complete_import writes the final state before swapping it in, so a failed
  write leaves the batch uploading and retryable; manifest and label writes
  retry briefly on Windows sharing errors; a failed flush no longer fails
  an upload that was stored; discard reads only finished manifests.
- The API token fails closed: without IMPS_API_TOKEN every route but
  /health is locked unless --no-api-token is given; smoke_runtime.ps1
  passes its own token.
- desktop:prepare falls through the Windows Store python alias (exit 9009).

Frontend
- Errors from import, Finish and Discard stay visible (the follow-up
  refresh no longer clears them); a folder import skips files the importer
  refuses instead of stopping; batch names stay within 120 characters as
  both the sidecar and the schema count them.
- Train Model: preview spinner and errors reset with the selection, AE and
  GRU window pools shown separately, requirement labels in Thai, refresh
  keeps the selection; Finish reports a batch that did not become ready.
- Ground Truth radios move with the arrow keys; the hotspot reason names
  the 20-session rule.

Tests: 60 Python (unreadable-manifest cleanup, ZIP64, retryable completion,
parallel uploads with discards), 223 vitest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
